{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnDataGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnDataGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnGeneral","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QSchurWeyl"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburnDataOfWeights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburnDataOfWeights","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnDataGeneral.lean#L92-L104","doc":"**`HeckeWedderburnData` for `H_{n+1}(q)`, at every `n`.**\n\nThe weight family `w` is an **input**.  `markov_eq` is true by `rfl`, because `markov` is *defined*\nas the weighted character sum — so this packages the block decomposition and says nothing about\nwhich `w` makes the functional a Markov trace.  See the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburnFin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburnFin","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnDataGeneral.lean#L75-L90","doc":"The Wedderburn isomorphism in `HeckeWedderburnData`'s indexing.\n\n`hq2` stays in the `q ^ 2 ≠ 1` form rather than being retyped to\n`GenericParameter.NotRootOfUnity`: this file is `ℝ`-typed throughout, where the two are\nequivalent (`GenericParameter.ofSqNeOne`), and `q ^ 2 ≠ 1` is what an `ℝ` caller naturally\nhas.  The conversion happens at the call, exactly as in `HeckeSemisimpleReal`.\n\n(The file carries a **pre-existing** §7c flag — `ℝ` in the types with no archimedean\nconstruct anywhere, measured 0 before and after this edit.  Generalising it is real work and\nis deliberately NOT done here: this is a main-red fix and widening it would bury the\none-line repair.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.blockFinReindex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.blockFinReindex","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnDataGeneral.lean#L64-L73","doc":"Reindex every block from its `SYT` index to `Fin d_λ`, the shape `HeckeWedderburnData` wants. ","signatureChunk":0}]}